	href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&display=swap"
	rel="stylesheet"
/>

<div class="section">
	<div class="content">
		<div class="title">
			<img src="/azurite.svg" id="logo" alt="Azurite logo" />
			<h1>AZURITE</h1>
		</div>

		<p>coming soon...</p>
	</div>
	<p class="scrolldown">scroll down...</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
	<div class="content">
		<div class="title">
			<img src="/about.svg" id="about" alt="About icon" />
			<h1>ABOUT THE PROJECT</h1>
		</div>

		<p>Azurite is a game engine that relies on only data and logic, using JSON for scenes, prefab, and configuration, and using Lua for all game logic. Azurite is designed for anyone, due to its simplistic design. Azurite is 2D and uses ECS for game objects, making games fast and easy to make, as every behavior consists of one block of JSON with bits of information for configuration. Azurite was designed for games like Typic Trials and Manufact Mania, both unreleased as of now.</p>
	</div>
</div>